description:
pkix-ct/src/verify.rs:130-151

```rust
/// ```no_run
/// # #[cfg(all(feature = "log-list", feature = "log-list-json"))]
/// # fn example() -> Result<(), pkix_ct::Error> {
/// use pkix_ct::{CtLogList, SctVerifier, SctList};
/// use pkix_path::DefaultVerifier;
/// ...
/// let v = SctVerifier::new(logs, DefaultVerifier);
/// ```
```

`pkix_path::DefaultVerifier` is feature-gated:

```rust
// pkix-path/src/lib.rs:4254
#[cfg(any(feature = "p256", feature = "p384", feature = "rsa"))]
pub struct DefaultVerifier;
```

`pkix-path`'s default features include `["rsa", "p256"]`, so under
default-feature builds `DefaultVerifier` IS available. But if a
downstream user builds `pkix-ct` with `default-features = false` on
`pkix-path` (or via workspace inheritance where the workspace
disables defaults), the doctest will fail to compile.

The `# #[cfg(all(feature = "log-list", feature = "log-list-json"))]`
gate only checks pkix-ct's features, not pkix-path's. The doctest
is hidden from invocation by the gate (so `no_run` doesn't matter)
but is the COMPILE step (rustdoc still compiles the doc-test code
under `cargo test --doc`).

Recommendation: tighten the gate, or switch to a verifier example
that doesn't depend on a pkix-path optional feature.

Option A (cheaper):

```rust
/// ```no_run
/// # #[cfg(all(feature = "log-list", feature = "log-list-json"))]
/// # fn example() -> Result<(), pkix_ct::Error> {
/// # struct StubVerifier;
/// # impl pkix_path::SignatureVerifier for StubVerifier { ... }
/// use pkix_ct::{CtLogList, SctVerifier};
/// let v = SctVerifier::new(logs, StubVerifier);
/// ```
```

A stub verifier is portable across pkix-path features.

Option B: add a doctest-features clause to Cargo.toml:

```toml
[[example]]
name = "verify_sct"
required-features = ["log-list-json", "pkix-path/p256"]
```

(Not exactly a doctest equivalent, but the same idea.)

Option C: keep current example, document the implicit feature
dependency:

```rust
/// # Feature requirements
///
/// This example requires `pkix-path`'s `p256` or `rsa` feature to
/// be enabled (both are in pkix-path's default feature set).
```

Priority P3 because in the typical setup the doctest compiles, but
a hardened CI matrix that turns off pkix-path defaults will fail.

This connects to PKIX-ppbr.28 (feature interactions) — the contract
between pkix-ct features and pkix-path features is under-documented.
